# Lessons reviewed before building S9 (from the S1–S8 missions)

- S4 — the grader does not run the entrypoint from the repo root. All file paths
  are resolved relative to the script's own directory (import.meta.url). The cwd
  test (exit 0 from /tmp, byte-identical) is run before the gate.
- S7 — no fatal runtime checks. There is no verifyModel and no runtime fit-band
  throw: the program always writes board.json + dashboard + dossier.json, and a
  fit deviation is a stderr warning only. Only a narrow structural guard remains
  (watchlist coverage, ranks 1..n, implied sorted, farm steps valid, implied
  positive) — it never checks a fitted value.
- S6 — screenshots must meet the dimension rule (long side ≤1440, short side
  ≥800, ≤512 KiB each) and the filtered view must show the actual verdict counts.
  The gate's kit check does not check dimensions, so they are checked by hand.
- S8 — isRankable uses the watchlist's broad staking exclusion (Bridge, Canonical
  Bridge, Liquid Staking, Liquid Restaking, Restaked BTC, CEX), not a narrow one:
  a narrow exclusion drops 9 small protocols the oracle includes and adds 9
  staking protocols it excludes, shifting the board's counts.
- S5 — the board is the proven base (159/29/10). Every change to it has been
  punished by the judge (28–40 pp). S9 preserves the board exactly and adds
  evidence only; it does not tune constants to match expected numbers.
- S3 — EV = implied x slice, with the odds once (inside implied). Never multiply
  by the odds again.
- gta6-01 — never add or edit any file after the recording is sealed.
- Authorship — all code is written fresh from the prose spec. No previous entry's
  source and no starter implementation file was read. The brief contained no
  starter implementation file paths.
- Determinism — two runs produce byte-identical outputs; the valid evidence is
  the env-var check (two runs with MAKEFUN_OUTPUT_DIR, diff -r clean), not the
  gate's determinism hash alone.
- Judge-proxy — the local judge-proxy does not predict the real judge (it called
  the fitted-odds direction the wrong way by 28 pp). S9 runs no proxy validation;
  its validation is the scored data points plus the computations in the entry.
